    "alert_id": "EX2_001",
    "title": "AKI likely pre-renal from gastroenteritis, not TDF toxicity",
    "message": "Guidelines note that intercurrent illnesses with dehydration or sepsis may cause renal deterioration in patients on TDF, requiring creatinine checking during hospital admissions. This patient has severe gastroenteritis with dehydration (BP 90/60, dry mucous membranes, reduced skin turgor), two affected family members suggesting infectious gastroenteritis, and a urea-to-creatinine ratio of 24:1 favouring pre-renal AKI. Urinalysis shows no protein or glucose, which argues against TDF-induced tubular toxicity. Baseline creatinine was normal (0.9) one year ago. The acute presentation over 5 days with hypovolaemia strongly supports pre-renal AKI rather than chronic TDF nephrotoxicity. Permanent discontinuation of TDF may be unnecessary if renal function recovers with fluid resuscitation.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Resuscitate with IV fluids and recheck creatinine before deciding on permanent TDF discontinuation. If renal function recovers, TDF may be continued with ongoing monitoring.",
