    "alert_id": "EX2_002",
    "title": "DTG creatinine rise algorithm does not apply to acute AKI",
    "message": "Guidelines describe a DTG-related creatinine rise algorithm for small, stable increases (<30 µmol/L) occurring within the first month of DTG initiation. This patient's creatinine rose from 0.9 to 2.4 mg/dL (increase ~133 µmol/L) after 2 years on DTG, which is far outside the DTG-related pattern. The magnitude and acuity are inconsistent with DTG-related creatinine elevation. This acute rise should be attributed to the gastroenteritis episode and managed with fluid resuscitation rather than DTG adjustment.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
